From b8644bde324e25404b3b5d8a6275e44a28717736 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PapyElGringo <adrien@pesler.be>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:06:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [flow] Do not damage texture layers whose texture has no new
 frame

TextureLayer::Diff marked its whole area dirty on every frame, since the
engine could not tell whether a texture had changed (TODO(knopp)). Any
frame, even one that only blinks a text cursor, repainted every texture
on screen, along with whatever is composited over or filters them: a blur
over a texture re-ran over the whole blurred area.

A texture can now identify the frame it presents (Texture::GetFrameId).
The embedder's GL, Metal and Vulkan textures do: they keep presenting
the same image until MarkNewFrameAvailable. Textures that may change on
any paint (Android's) keep the default, std::nullopt, and are damaged on
every frame as before.

The diff records the frame each texture layer painted in the layer tree,
next to its paint regions (a retained layer instance belongs to several
trees, so it cannot be stored in the layer), and a texture layer that
paints the same texture frame at the same place adds no damage.
Frame identifiers are unique across textures, so a texture registered
again under the same id is damaged.
